# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL WEIGHTS -- never in git
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A LoRA adapter is 110-126 MB and GitHub rejects any single file over 100 MB,
# so lemmatizer_lora_qwen/adapter_model.safetensors (115 MB) cannot be pushed
# at all. Nor should it be: weights are a build output, reproducible from
# unsloth/data/*.jsonl by train.py, and re-uploading a new copy on every
# retrain would bloat the history permanently even after deletion.
#
# Share them out of band instead -- Google Drive, which already holds them
# from the Colab run -- and import with:
#     python import_adapters.py --from "<drive folder>"
unsloth/lemmatizer_lora_*/
adapters/
*.safetensors

# Training checkpoints. The trainer writes a full adapter copy per checkpoint,
# so these are the same weights again, several times over. plot_training.py
# only ever reads trainer_state.json out of them, and that file is kept.
unsloth/training_runs/**/checkpoint-*/
!unsloth/training_runs/**/checkpoint-*/trainer_state.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED, AND CHEAP TO REGENERATE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
unsloth_compiled_cache/
figures/

# Model predictions: ~30 KB each, regenerated by crawl/evaluate.py --model.
# Kept OUT because they are only valid for the exact adapter that produced
# them, and a stale cache scored against a retrained adapter would report the
# old model's numbers as the new one's.
data/model_predictions_*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL NOISE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
~$*                 # Excel lock files, created whenever a sheet is open
*.log
*.bak
.env                # the YouTube API key lives here; never commit it
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY TRACKED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything else, about 54 MB, and all of it is the project rather than its
# build output:
#
#   data/*.jsonl              the corpus, silver, gold, val -- the dataset
#   data/*.xlsx               the labelling sheets, as annotated
#   unsloth/data/*.jsonl      the training targets
#   malindo_morph/            the dictionary the rule baseline depends on
#   *.py, crawl/*.py          the pipeline
#   *.ipynb                   the Colab training notebook
#
# The largest tracked file is malindo_dic_2024.tsv at 16 MB, well inside the
# limit. Nothing here is regenerable without re-crawling YouTube, which cannot
# be reproduced -- comments get edited and deleted -- so it all belongs in git.
